<title>USA: N.Y. MTA $383 mln bonds repriced, yields raised.</title>
<headline>N.Y. MTA $383 mln bonds repriced, yields raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. said Wednesday it repriced Metropolitan Transportation Authority, N.Y.'s $383 million bond deal, raising yields in several maturities and lifting the top yield in 2027 to 5.98 percent from 5.95 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>METROPOLITAN TRANSPORTATION AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $382,910,000*</p>
<p>$196,915,000 COMMUTER FACILITIES REVENUE BONDS,</p>
<p>$185,995,000 TRANSIT FACILITIES REVENUE BONDS,</p>
<p>SERIES 1997A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.  NO NEW ORDERS WILL BE ACCEPTED.</p>
